1
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,040
I forgot to tell you. We're not having dinner at home

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,440
this New Year's.

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:10,600
How long did you plan on keeping this from me?

4
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,000
I won't let that homewrecker

5
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,920
disrespect my mom ever again.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,360
Please have all the necessary paperwork

7
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,320
ready for me to sign.

8
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:19,640
I'm leaving today.

9
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:20,360
P'Piang,

10
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,360
where's P'Ing?

11
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:22,880
I've been waiting for you

12
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:23,960
to come home.

13
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:25,720
Who do you think you are,

14
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:26,880
messing with my boy?

15
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,520
I've got proof that Itt framed P'Phet.

16
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,080
What makes you think I'd trust you this time?

17
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:44,800
P'Ing...

18
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:47,480
I love you.

19
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,440
After tonight...

20
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:54,640
you'll finally be mine.

21
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,440
Just now, he and I...

22
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,480
were together...

23
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,560
in bed.

24
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:19,360
Those shrimp look delicious.

25
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,400
Let me peel them for you.

26
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,120
P'Ing,

27
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,560
are you free on the night of the 20th?

28
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,000
I'd like to take you out for dinner.

29
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,240
There's nothing going on between you two, right?

30
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:26,920
This one's for you, P'Ing.

31
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,000
What's going on between you and P'Ing?

32
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,320
But if you want to date P'Ing,

33
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:30,000
I just want to warn you

34
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:30,960
that he never loves anyone.

35
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,880
I'm afraid you'll get hurt.

36
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,040
You're not running away

37
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,360
just because you fell for my brother, are you?

38
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,880
I've only ever asked you for one thing.

39
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:37,800
After all, you have a share in this, too.

40
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,640
That sentence you didn't get to finish...

41
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,000
You'd say you liked me, right?

42
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:48,320
Itt,

43
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:50,120
why would you do this?

44
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,960
How could you do this?

45
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,000
He's your damn brother.

46
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,040
So what?

47
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,000
I've loved him this whole time.

48
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,000
Long before you ever did.

49
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:02,680
Itt, you...

50
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:14,040
He was so amazing in bed.

51
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,800
Damn you.

52
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,320
Goddammit.

53
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,240
You piece of...

54
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,440
He's your brother.

55
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:27,440
Itt, he's your freaking brother.

56
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,960
He's your brother.

57
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:29,840
You little...

58
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:30,560
Damn you.

59
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:33,120
How could I have ever trusted someone like you?

60
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:34,720
You disgusting creep.

61
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:36,560
Goddammit.

62
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,240
He's your brother.

63
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:40,720
Go to hell, you piece of trash.

64
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,200
You sick animal.

65
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:50,600
That's enough.

66
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:13,800
P'Ing.

67
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,200
P'Ing...

68
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:26,960
I'm so sorry.

69
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,159
Let me untie you.

70
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:42,800
I'll untie you right now...

71
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:50,520
I'm really sorry.

72
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,159
I'll get these ropes off you.

73
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,360
Don't touch me.

74
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,960
You're not even mine yet.

75
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:51,560
Please just give me a chance.

76
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,320
I love you,

77
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:55,400
P'Ing.

78
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,200
Just go to hell.

79
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,040
Don't ever show your face to me again.

80
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,160
If you ever mess with him again,

81
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:18,760
I'll kill you.

82
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,280
P'Ing.

83
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:41,360
Hey.

84
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,400
Please come home with me.

85
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:44,480
P'Ing...

86
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:46,160
I'm sorry.

87
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,160
-Come home with me. -Let go.

88
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,040
Let go of me.

89
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:51,840
P'Ing...

90
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,440
-P'Ing... -Get off me.

91
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:57,400
P'Ing...

92
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:58,520
Hey.

93
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,360
Please put the jacket on.

94
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:04,120
Come home with me.

95
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,760
I don't want to.

96
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:10,600
-P'Ing, please. -Get lost.

97
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:14,160
I'm sorry. I really deserve to die.

98
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:15,200
Let's go home.

99
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:18,960
Get off me.

100
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,280
Yok...

101
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,560
Someone like you...

102
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:34,200
is so damn selfish.

103
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,760
You're absolutely disgusting.

104
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,440
Let me tell you something.

105
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,760
You...

106
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:49,360
are the last person I ever want to see.

107
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,560
And if you have any decency left,

108
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,840
don't show your face to me again.

109
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,320
P'Ing...

110
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,280
From now on,

111
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,240
you must take good care of your younger brother.

112
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,480
He's my brother. Only I can mess with him.

113
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:54,920
P'Ing...

114
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:56,000
I love you.

115
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:56,720
P'Ing.

116
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:57,720
P'Ing...

117
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,600
After tonight...

118
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,520
you'll finally be mine.

119
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,280
-P'Ing. -Please come home with me.

120
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,000
-P'Ing. -How could you do this?

121
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,160
He's your damn brother.

122
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:06,920
I love you.

123
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:07,440
I love you...

124
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,040
-So what? -P'Ing...

125
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:09,040
-Leave me alone. -P'Ing.

126
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,200
I've loved him this whole time.

127
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,440
Long before you ever did.

128
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,720
Are you home yet, Mr. Ing?

129
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,200
I'm home.

130
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:37,120
Where are you, Junior?

131
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,360
I was worried you'd forget to eat again,

132
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:44,800
so I left some food for you in the fridge.

133
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:49,440
-Okay. -Just heat it up, and it's ready to eat.

134
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,520
Hurry back.

135
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,920
I miss you.

136
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,440
I will.

137
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:04,600
I'll be there as soon as I can.

138
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:08,800
P'Ing.

139
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,120
Dammit.

140
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:20,800
P'Ing.

141
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:23,800
P'Ing, it's me.

142
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,320
P'Ing.

143
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,600
Hey.

144
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,680
It's me.

145
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:46,160
Hello?

146
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:47,640
P'Ing.

147
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,600
Hey, P'Ing.

148
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:53,480
Yeah.

149
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:56,280
How do you like my new haircut?

150
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:58,280
I know it's different,

151
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:00,360
but it'll grow on you.

152
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:02,080
Close the door, you brat.

153
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,680
That haircut actually suits you.

154
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,880
I brought a ton of stuff for you.

155
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,600
How can you live in a place like this?

156
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:15,880
It's tiny.

157
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:17,640
The design is so weird.

158
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,920
And it's so dark in here.

159
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,600
Let me get some light in here.

160
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,120
That's better.

161
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:32,600
Come on, P'Ing.

162
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,160
I'm so sorry.

163
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,800
You can beat me up if you want.

164
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,280
Just kick the crap out of me.

165
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:39,960
Beat me until you're satisfied.

166
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,160
Just let me make it up to you.

167
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,080
Hey, Pite.

168
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,000
How did you know I was here?

169
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:49,960
I waited for you at Grandpa's.

170
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:51,920
I figured if Grandpa was there,

171
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:53,640
you might go easier on me,

172
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,200
but you never showed up.

173
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,680
Grandpa then gave me your new address

174
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,360
and asked me to give this stuff to you.

175
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:59,640
So I decided...

176
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:00,560
"Okay,

177
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,720
I'll let you beat me up as hard as you want."

178
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:04,800
But at the very least,

179
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:07,440
I had to get my apology out.

180
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:10,240
Oh, fine.

181
00:17:16,079 --> 00:17:17,359
Are you sick?

182
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,680
Are you okay?

183
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:22,960
Whoa, you're burning up.

184
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,119
Are you living here all alone?

185
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:26,560
Don't you have a maid?

186
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:27,520
Pite.

187
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,480
Yeah?

188
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:30,920
Can you please shut the hell up?

189
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,520
You should get some rest.

190
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:33,440
Do you have any medicine?

191
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:34,840
I brought some with me,

192
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:36,800
but you have to eat something first.

193
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:37,600
Tell you what.

194
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,880
I'll whip up some food for you.

195
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:39,800
What do you want?

196
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,840
I'll take care of everything.

197
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:43,480
Do you want a snack first?

198
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,000
Grandpa bought a whole bunch of stuff.

199
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,080
What looks good to you?

200
00:17:46,240 --> 00:17:46,920
How about some fried bananas?

201
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,360
I think you'll like them.

202
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:50,120
Here, eat these while you wait.

203
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:51,080
I'll be right back

204
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:52,280
with some real food.

205
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:53,680
Whoa.

206
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:54,840
P'Ing.

207
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:56,600
I'm trying to sleep.

208
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:58,200
Just wait for me.

209
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,400
I'll whip something up for you.

210
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:01,040
What do I have to work with here?

211
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:03,600
What do you want for this meal?

212
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,640
-Want it spicy? -Dammit.

213
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:07,400
Or something sweet?

214
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:18,560
Who's that?

215
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,240
Itt?

216
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,280
What happened?

217
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,440
Should we go to the doctor?

218
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:39,880
Well, come on in.

219
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:41,400
I'll make you something to eat.

220
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:47,720
Please forgive me.

221
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:48,600
What?

222
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:51,080
Please forgive me, P'Ing.

223
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,480
It's not like you've even been drinking.

224
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:58,600
Open your damn eyes. I'm not your brother.

225
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:03,200
I shouldn't have been so impulsive.

226
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:05,560
But it's all your fault.

227
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,200
Why is he the only one you ever see?

228
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:10,120
Why can't you look at me for once?

229
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,680
Itt, what the hell are you doing?

230
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,920
Are you using me as a stand-in for your brother?

231
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:22,480
I should have found a better place...

232
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:25,480
to lock you up forever.

233
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:29,320
Get off.

234
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,600
Have you lost your mind?

235
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,520
Where am I?

236
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,040
Is anyone there?

237
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:09,920
Help.

238
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,720
You're finally awake.

239
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:23,720
Would you like something to eat?

240
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:25,720
Itt,

241
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,840
what are you doing to me?

242
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,800
What's with this suit you put on me?

243
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,400
I even made your favorite dish, P'Ing.

244
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,360
I hate shrimp.

245
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:39,000
No.

246
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,000
You love it.

247
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,840
Just take a bite.

248
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:55,440
What exactly do you want, Itt?

249
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:59,080
I just want you to stay with me.

250
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,960
I'm not your brother, Itt.

251
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:04,680
You are now.

252
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:08,120
Here you go.

253
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:09,280
Have some khao soi.

254
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,800
I got a huge piece of chicken for you,

255
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:13,040
so you can eat up

256
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,200
and get well soon.

257
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,040
Hey.

258
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,480
Who on earth taught you

259
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,960
to put a whole slice of lime in it?

260
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,120
Well, I saw it served that way online.

261
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:29,280
Come on.

262
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:30,800
I think it'll actually taste better.

263
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:32,320
You know, it'll make it more flavorful.

264
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:33,400
Eat up.

265
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:35,960
Hurry, and tell me what you think.

266
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,000
P'Ing,

267
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,920
I didn't really understand what was going on.

268
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,080
I'm sorry

269
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,760
for always being such a burden to you.

270
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:53,920
But now...

271
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,680
I want to help you, too.

272
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:59,080
Just say the word,

273
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:01,200
and I'll deal with Itt and Yok.

274
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:02,720
You can leave those jerks to me.

275
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:04,600
That's enough.

276
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:07,800
Why?

277
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:08,880
It won't be long

278
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,360
before you head back to the army, right?

279
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:12,840
Just don't cause any more trouble.

280
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:15,960
I'll stay for as long...

281
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:18,080
as you want me to.

282
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:18,840
Hey,

283
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:21,040
I'm pretty good at fighting now.

284
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:25,200
I'll just take care of those jerks

285
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,360
in some dark alley.

286
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,520
No one will know it was me.

287
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:29,440
Stop talking so much.

288
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,480
Just eat your food.

289
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:31,920
Oh,

290
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:34,680
finish this, too.

291
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:36,600
What? You're not eating anymore?

292
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:38,160
One look is all I need.

293
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:39,920
It's inedible.

294
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,640
P'Ing...

295
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:53,080
It actually tastes pretty good.

296
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:54,760
Right.

297
00:22:55,920 --> 00:22:56,960
Hey.

298
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:59,200
Once you're feeling better,

299
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,520
let's go out.

300
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:03,400
Yeah. Sure.

301
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:04,600
Really?

302
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:05,720
Yes.

303
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,120
Then...

304
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:08,320
let's go to a bar.

305
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,800
That one favorite bar of yours.

306
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:11,440
New year, new life.

307
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,400
Sounds good?

308
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:13,520
You coming?

309
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,240
-Yeah... -Let's do it tonight.

310
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:19,560
You little brat.

311
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:20,560
Just a walk

312
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:21,960
around the neighborhood is enough.

313
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:24,160
Can't you see I'm sick?

314
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:25,760
Going to a bar?

315
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:27,440
Are you trying to kill me?

316
00:23:28,480 --> 00:23:29,800
Fine, a walk it is.

317
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,600
Let's go right now.

318
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:36,600
-Come on, let's go for a walk. -Jeez.

319
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:40,760
P'Ing, put some muscle into it.

320
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:42,680
-Fine. -Stop acting like you have no strength.

321
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:44,200
-What? -Help me out here.

322
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,080
Help me.

323
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:47,040
Put some muscle into it, huh?

324
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:49,800
-P'Ing. -Dammit.

325
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:51,960
-Just because I'm a little sick… -You just kicked me.

326
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:54,080
Come on, let's go. Please?

327
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:55,320
I don't wanna stay cooped up in this room.

328
00:23:55,760 --> 00:23:56,840
Fine.

329
00:23:57,840 --> 00:23:59,880
What a lovely brother you are.

330
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,960
Let me see. Looking good?

331
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,600
You look amazing.

332
00:24:07,640 --> 00:24:09,480
You might find someone who's your type. Let's go.

333
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:55,320
Why don't you just do as you're told?

334
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:58,160
Dammit.

335
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:04,120
I'm a human being.

336
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:07,560
How could you use me to replace someone else?

337
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:30,800
Why do you have to run?

338
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:36,000
Why won't you look at me?

339
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:41,280
Why can't you just stay by my side?

340
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:42,680
Get out.

341
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:44,200
Leave me alone.

342
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:46,320
-Why do you have to run from me? -Get off me.

343
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:47,920
Why do you want to run away?

344
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:49,320
Stay away from me.

345
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:54,640
P'Ing.

346
00:25:57,360 --> 00:25:58,120
P'Ing...

347
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,560
I'm sorry, P'Ing.

348
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:12,200
Why are you making me do this?

349
00:26:15,600 --> 00:26:17,360
Why won't you ever look at me?

350
00:26:18,360 --> 00:26:19,640
All these years...

351
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:24,000
I've been waiting for you to see me.

352
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:26,720
Listen,

353
00:26:28,320 --> 00:26:30,360
when someone starts feeling like...

354
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,600
the whole world has done them wrong,

355
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:33,920
it's usually because...

356
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:36,520
they themselves

357
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:37,880
are the problem.

358
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:44,520
All these plants and puddles...

359
00:26:44,560 --> 00:26:46,920
God, these damn mosquitoes are everywhere.

360
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:53,360
Can you just stop moving?

361
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,800
Wait, forgive me.

362
00:26:59,800 --> 00:27:00,560
P'Ing...

363
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:04,200
Oh, look at this brat.

364
00:27:04,280 --> 00:27:05,560
What the hell are you doing here?

365
00:27:05,840 --> 00:27:07,120
Go back the way you came.

366
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:08,080
Get lost.

367
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:13,240
I just wanted to see how you were doing.

368
00:27:14,520 --> 00:27:17,160
And do you think I want to see you?

369
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:19,360
I've been waiting for you all day.

370
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:20,320
Hold on.

371
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:26,440
I told you to stay away from him. Piss off.

372
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:28,200
I just got back from the army, you know.

373
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:30,160
Come at me, you jerk.

374
00:27:30,560 --> 00:27:31,640
I'm sorry.

375
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:39,920
P'Ing, hey.

376
00:27:46,280 --> 00:27:47,200
Where's Pite?

377
00:27:48,440 --> 00:27:49,440
What did you do to him?

378
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:51,600
I didn't do anything.

379
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:54,520
P'Ing, I missed you.

380
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:55,920
Don't touch me.

381
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:58,440
Just because I used to like you,

382
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:00,400
does that mean I owe you something?

383
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:05,200
I'm the one who owes you.

384
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,400
P'Ing...

385
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:11,720
You want to make it up to me?

386
00:28:12,560 --> 00:28:14,120
If that's what you're trying to do,

387
00:28:15,080 --> 00:28:17,160
just get the hell out of my life.

388
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,800
How could I ever do that?

389
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:21,560
Aren't you the reason

390
00:28:21,560 --> 00:28:23,080
I can't live without you anymore?

391
00:28:23,120 --> 00:28:24,400
Oh, really?

392
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:27,080
But now, I just want you to die.

393
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,200
P'Ing,

394
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,960
we've already come this far.

395
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:43,600
Let me go.

396
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:45,840
I even got the rings you threw away.

397
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:48,360
It means fate doesn't want us to end things yet.

398
00:28:58,680 --> 00:28:59,720
These rings?

399
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:02,200
I just bought them on a whim.

400
00:29:03,560 --> 00:29:05,640
Don't think you're so special.

401
00:29:07,360 --> 00:29:09,240
They mean absolutely nothing to me.

402
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:12,600
Don't get the wrong idea.

403
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:26,440
You jerk.

404
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:29,080
You've really put me through hell.

405
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:32,280
Go without me. I'll handle this.

406
00:29:39,040 --> 00:29:41,080
What do you want? A fight?

407
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,560
What the hell?

408
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:43,880
Stop.

409
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:47,680
Stop it.

410
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:49,000
Leave him alone.

411
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:49,960
Stop it.

412
00:29:50,560 --> 00:29:51,760
Hey, stop.

413
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:11,200
What now?

414
00:30:24,640 --> 00:30:26,240
What's the deal between you and him?

415
00:30:27,200 --> 00:30:28,160
Are you guys dating?

416
00:30:29,120 --> 00:30:29,960
Answer me.

417
00:30:32,800 --> 00:30:33,680
Damn.

418
00:30:34,480 --> 00:30:36,080
Poor him.

419
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:40,080
He shouldn't have fallen for someone who looks like you.

420
00:30:40,320 --> 00:30:42,200
Besides those good looks,

421
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:43,920
everything else about you is trash.

422
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:49,480
Look.

423
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:52,320
Let me tell you something.

424
00:30:55,280 --> 00:30:56,680
This company...

425
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:00,680
almost went under once.

426
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:06,000
It was P'Ing who managed to save it,

427
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:09,240
only for all those relatives to keep leeching off him,

428
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:12,080
yet not a single person ever stood by him.

429
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:17,680
That's how it is.

430
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:20,320
But if you ask me...

431
00:31:21,680 --> 00:31:22,680
it's for the best

432
00:31:23,080 --> 00:31:24,920
that he doesn't have to deal with this company anymore.

433
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:28,720
It's not even worth his sweat and tears.

434
00:31:32,480 --> 00:31:33,200
Hey.

435
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:35,880
The actual mistake you made

436
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:39,800
was helping that mother and son.

437
00:31:40,920 --> 00:31:42,240
P'Ing once told me...

438
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:44,640
he never hurt her or Itt.

439
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:47,280
That's true.

440
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:51,200
But I guess P'Ing and Itt never told you

441
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:54,400
who the real victim was.

442
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:00,920
If it hadn't been for that day...

443
00:32:04,360 --> 00:32:07,280
when that pregnant woman came and made a scene,

444
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:10,640
driving P'Ing's mom to despair,

445
00:32:12,760 --> 00:32:14,600
she wouldn't have left us so soon.

446
00:32:21,800 --> 00:32:23,440
After his mom passed away,

447
00:32:25,520 --> 00:32:27,320
my mom wanted to take him in,

448
00:32:29,040 --> 00:32:30,200
but he wouldn't let her.

449
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:33,840
Come on, Ing. Let's go visit your mom.

450
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:35,880
I had so much fun shopping today.

451
00:32:35,920 --> 00:32:38,200
Hey, help me with these bags.

452
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:40,240
-My arms are aching. -Yes, ma'am.

453
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:41,200
You...

454
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:45,080
Today is the anniversary of Ravipa's death,

455
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:49,200
and you chose to spend the day enjoying yourself?

456
00:32:49,560 --> 00:32:51,280
Why would you say such a thing?

457
00:32:51,680 --> 00:32:54,200
Since when do you have to schedule when to be happy?

458
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:55,360
Shameless.

459
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:57,200
You have no shame.

460
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:58,920
What's going on?

461
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,840
Honey.

462
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:03,280
What happened? Is something the matter?

463
00:33:03,320 --> 00:33:04,200
Triyot,

464
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:07,880
Ravipa has only been gone for a short while,

465
00:33:08,880 --> 00:33:11,600
and you brought this mistress and her son into this house

466
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:13,360
so you all could enjoy yourselves?

467
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:16,320
My, you all look incredibly happy, don't you?

468
00:33:18,120 --> 00:33:19,200
What about Ing?

469
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:22,120
He's your own flesh and blood.

470
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:25,920
What did my nephew do to deserve this?

471
00:33:27,440 --> 00:33:29,840
Come on. Let's go visit your mom.

472
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,240
It's okay.

473
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:36,520
-I just went shopping. -Don't pay them any mind.

474
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:43,360
P'Ing said that...

475
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:46,320
if he moved into my house,

476
00:33:46,520 --> 00:33:49,560
his mom and his real home would be lost forever,

477
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:52,960
so he wanted to take back everything

478
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:55,840
that rightfully belonged to him.

479
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:00,920
It's such a shame, though,

480
00:34:02,280 --> 00:34:04,280
that he was too kind to those two

481
00:34:05,680 --> 00:34:07,880
even though he had every reason to be ruthless.

482
00:34:15,719 --> 00:34:18,719
I never saw him happy again after that.

483
00:34:29,120 --> 00:34:31,600
The last time he truly smiled was probably...

484
00:34:34,560 --> 00:34:36,000
when this photo was taken.

485
00:34:37,600 --> 00:34:38,880
What the hell are you doing?

486
00:34:38,920 --> 00:34:39,960
Give it back.

487
00:34:40,159 --> 00:34:42,719
I'm taking this. You can just ask him for a new one.

488
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:44,679
What is wrong with you? Are you a stalker or something?

489
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:47,280
Hey. Get back here.

490
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:51,280
Consider yourself dismissed.

491
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:01,840
Where are you, Yok?

492
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:03,240
I...

493
00:35:04,280 --> 00:35:06,880
Dad wants to see you. Come back right now.

494
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:07,560
Okay.

495
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:18,520
We need to launch

496
00:35:18,560 --> 00:35:20,520
three real estate developments simultaneously.

497
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,240
Construction will begin in phases

498
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,480
to capture market share

499
00:35:23,520 --> 00:35:24,880
in areas with demand

500
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:28,120
and drive customers into our hotel business.

501
00:35:28,440 --> 00:35:29,360
He's clearly scrapping

502
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:31,000
all of Mr. Ing's plans

503
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:32,760
and just doing whatever he wants.

504
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:35,680
Ms. Mithuna.

505
00:35:37,840 --> 00:35:39,720
I'm appointing you as Group Vice President

506
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:41,360
to oversee the projects.

507
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:46,440
And Mrs. Arisara...

508
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:58,120
She will be in charge of investment and management.

509
00:35:58,200 --> 00:36:00,080
So he's bringing his mom in as a shareholder?

510
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:01,960
I assure you...

511
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:04,120
that Mrs. Arisara's involvement

512
00:36:04,720 --> 00:36:07,160
will not impact your interests negatively

513
00:36:08,200 --> 00:36:09,560
because my goal

514
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:11,920
is to make Araya Group's share of the pie

515
00:36:11,960 --> 00:36:13,000
grow even larger.

516
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:15,160
Understood, Mr. Itt.

517
00:36:15,240 --> 00:36:17,320
We have full confidence in you.

518
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:18,680
Excellent.

519
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:20,640
If you think it's appropriate,

520
00:36:20,640 --> 00:36:22,120
then so be it.

521
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:34,960
I'd like to resign.

522
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:53,520
Then that's settled.

523
00:36:54,560 --> 00:36:56,000
If anyone else wishes to resign,

524
00:36:56,600 --> 00:36:57,760
please feel free to do so.

525
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:11,680
P'Ing...

526
00:37:13,680 --> 00:37:14,880
I've won.

527
00:37:18,640 --> 00:37:22,160
I've finally made my mom proud.

528
00:37:23,480 --> 00:37:24,440
In the past,

529
00:37:25,840 --> 00:37:27,880
you never even acknowledged us.

530
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:31,440
You never paid me any attention.

531
00:37:35,520 --> 00:37:36,880
But back then,

532
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:40,160
did you ever imagine

533
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,920
that you'd end up beneath me?

534
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:04,080
But why...

535
00:38:06,640 --> 00:38:08,280
Why am I not happy at all?

536
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:11,480
You know what?

537
00:38:12,680 --> 00:38:14,760
I was hoping you'd show up at the office today

538
00:38:16,640 --> 00:38:18,040
to ruin my presentation.

539
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:20,280
Why won't you ever look at me?

540
00:38:27,480 --> 00:38:29,280
Why aren't you here by my side?

541
00:38:40,720 --> 00:38:41,720
This is the last piece.

542
00:38:41,720 --> 00:38:43,280
We'll be heading out now.

543
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:12,400
Hello?

544
00:40:12,440 --> 00:40:13,440
Hello, Mr. Ing.

545
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:15,640
-It's Phet. -I know.

546
00:40:16,520 --> 00:40:18,320
I want to talk to you about my brother.

547
00:40:19,720 --> 00:40:20,560
Mr. Phet,

548
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:23,400
do you know what I want to hear about the least?

549
00:40:24,520 --> 00:40:26,520
Anything that mentions a brother.

550
00:40:27,160 --> 00:40:29,080
Whether it's your brother or mine,

551
00:40:29,080 --> 00:40:30,120
I don't want to hear it.

552
00:40:30,120 --> 00:40:31,720
You were dating Yok, weren't you?

553
00:40:39,920 --> 00:40:40,560
Yes.

554
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:42,320
Why?

555
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:44,040
Mr. Ing,

556
00:40:44,560 --> 00:40:47,040
I don't judge people for their personal lives,

557
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:50,920
but Yok is years younger than you.

558
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,120
Younger?

559
00:40:55,240 --> 00:40:56,160
What's so funny?

560
00:40:57,560 --> 00:40:58,840
Is it that funny?

561
00:40:58,920 --> 00:41:00,600
My brother openly told everyone in the family

562
00:41:00,640 --> 00:41:01,880
that he's in love with you.

563
00:41:06,640 --> 00:41:08,760
My father is so furious he hasn't eaten all day.

564
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:11,480
Wait a second.

565
00:41:14,320 --> 00:41:15,680
Did Yok really do that?

566
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:20,440
He actually had the nerve

567
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:21,920
to tell everyone he loves me?

568
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:22,800
Mr. Ing,

569
00:41:23,520 --> 00:41:25,160
do you think I'm joking?

570
00:41:27,560 --> 00:41:28,360
Yok.

571
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:29,880
Yok, why are you such a mess?

572
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:31,760
Go take a shower, son.

573
00:41:32,920 --> 00:41:33,960
Don't be nervous.

574
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:35,960
Uncle Wanchai has known you since you were a kid.

575
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:38,280
It's just a casual dinner.

576
00:41:39,440 --> 00:41:40,400
Hurry it up, Yok.

577
00:41:40,400 --> 00:41:41,880
Traffic is bad. We don't want to be late.

578
00:41:42,560 --> 00:41:44,120
Who's messaging me?

579
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:45,440
Oh...

580
00:41:45,440 --> 00:41:47,240
The minister sent a message saying

581
00:41:47,280 --> 00:41:48,360
he'll be a little late.

582
00:41:49,600 --> 00:41:51,640
We'd better get there a little early

583
00:41:51,640 --> 00:41:52,920
since we're taking his time.

584
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:54,040
That sounds good.

585
00:41:56,360 --> 00:41:57,360
I'm not going.

586
00:42:00,600 --> 00:42:01,760
Stop right there.

587
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:08,440
All this time,

588
00:42:08,560 --> 00:42:11,280
we've worked hard to give you every opportunity in life.

589
00:42:11,720 --> 00:42:12,600
And what have you done?

590
00:42:12,680 --> 00:42:15,640
Have you ever acted like you deserve to be in this family?

591
00:42:16,040 --> 00:42:16,800
Yok...

592
00:42:23,560 --> 00:42:24,480
Dad,

593
00:42:24,720 --> 00:42:25,640
Mom,

594
00:42:26,120 --> 00:42:27,000
P'Phet...

595
00:42:27,480 --> 00:42:29,640
There's something we need to talk about openly.

596
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:34,040
I already have someone I love,

597
00:42:35,320 --> 00:42:36,600
and I want to be with him.

598
00:42:37,600 --> 00:42:39,040
That's what I want to do.

599
00:42:41,560 --> 00:42:42,720
In fact,

600
00:42:43,680 --> 00:42:45,320
I've loved P'Ing for a long time.

601
00:43:08,160 --> 00:43:09,560
If there's anything else, just say it.

602
00:43:10,640 --> 00:43:12,960
I don't want to dig up the past with you.

603
00:43:15,160 --> 00:43:16,880
I'm just asking you to come here

604
00:43:18,560 --> 00:43:20,640
and make things clear to Yok face-to-face.

605
00:43:21,800 --> 00:43:23,840
Tell him to move on and admit his mistake.

606
00:43:24,640 --> 00:43:26,320
It'll be for the best for everyone.

607
00:43:29,120 --> 00:43:30,000
I'm not going.

608
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:32,200
You can't just run away from your responsibilities.

609
00:43:32,840 --> 00:43:34,760
Yok won't listen to anyone.

610
00:43:35,480 --> 00:43:37,080
He's even given up on his studies.

611
00:43:38,440 --> 00:43:39,600
And my father

612
00:43:40,200 --> 00:43:42,240
will never agree to compromise.

613
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:45,560
I'm begging you to help me.

614
00:43:46,880 --> 00:43:47,800
Please.

615
00:44:26,520 --> 00:44:27,400
Mr. Ing.

616
00:44:27,400 --> 00:44:29,880
I'm just a nobody with no job now.

617
00:44:30,040 --> 00:44:31,600
Don't sell yourself short, Mr. Ing.

618
00:44:31,680 --> 00:44:34,480
My life's been pretty damn exciting, Mom.

619
00:44:34,680 --> 00:44:36,880
I'm nothing but a pathetic loser.

620
00:44:37,400 --> 00:44:38,560
If you were still here,

621
00:44:38,720 --> 00:44:40,560
would you see me as one, too?

622
00:44:41,160 --> 00:44:42,560
Are you that into him?

623
00:44:43,040 --> 00:44:43,960
Listen to me.

624
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:45,200
Back when I was crazy about you,

625
00:44:45,200 --> 00:44:46,400
you found me disgusting.

626
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:47,640
And what are we now?

627
00:44:47,640 --> 00:44:48,960
You'd better make things clear with your brother

628
00:44:48,960 --> 00:44:49,680
and figure out what to do.

629
00:44:49,720 --> 00:44:51,040
Just stay the hell out of my life.

630
00:44:51,080 --> 00:44:52,760
What does he have that I don't?

631
00:44:54,080 --> 00:44:55,240
It's been a while.

632
00:44:55,320 --> 00:44:56,200
I promise

633
00:44:56,200 --> 00:44:57,800
I won't let myself be weak again.

634
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:59,640
[The UNCUT version of Fool in Love]

635
00:44:58,200 --> 00:45:00,640
I'll take back everything that's mine.

636
00:44:59,640 --> 00:45:02,800
[is exclusively available on iQIYI and iQ.com]
